/* Cross-ISO mechanism matrix — NWPP shard (rule 28 [R-MECH-MATRIX]).
 *
 * This file is NWPP's COLUMN of the matrix: one line per mechanism id
 * (the row set lives in ../mechanism-matrix.js, which carries the
 * mechanism-level id/cat/name/def/mode/note). A session that tests a
 * mechanism in NWPP updates ONLY this file — the cell verdict, the
 * forecast-lane posture (fc), the evidence citation (ev) and any
 * NWPP-specific note — plus the keeper/gates stamps on promotion.
 * Never edit another ISO's shard (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]): a verdict
 * transfers to no other ISO; candidates enter the target shard as U.
 *
 * Cell codes (same vocabulary as the base header): K keeper, R rejected,
 * I inert, G governance-refused/closed, O open, U untested, . n/a.
 * `fc` is the forecast-lane posture where it DIFFERS from the backcast
 * cell (omitted = same as cell). `ev` is this ISO's evidence citation.
 *
 * SEEDED AT NWPP-21 (2026-09-13), the NINTH shard — mechanical emission,
 * NO VERDICT MINTED. Measured at this lane's own base sha rather than taken
 * from its charter (plan §0: a sibling program may register first) — and the
 * charter's count was in fact overtaken. At the first emission (base sha
 * 33a7c961) the base `isos` carried SEVEN entries and NWPP was the eighth; on
 * the rebase (base sha b485b6af) SOCO-21 had landed as the eighth with ev
 * letter "O", so this column was RE-COUNTED and NWPP is the NINTH. It takes
 * ev letter "W" (E C P M N Q S O are taken). The re-count is the point: gate
 * G2 and plan §8.0 rule 3 exist for exactly this, and no count in this file
 * was carried forward from the charter. NWPP is NOT REGISTERED at this commit —
 * `config/iso_configs._ISO_BUILDERS` carries seven keys and W2 / NWPP-20
 * flips the pin — so there is no keeper, no bundle and no solve of any kind,
 * and `keeper` and `gates` are deliberately EMPTY.
 * Charter: docs/multi-iso/nwpp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row
 * NWPP-21 (the lever queue it seeds is §4 there and
 * docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.9); record
 * docs/handoffs/FINDING-nwpp-21-2026-09-13.md.
 *
 * THE CLASSIFICATION RULE, applied in this order (so a later lane can audit
 * any cell without re-deriving the whole column):
 *   (a) ISO-EXCLUSIVE ELSEWHERE -> `.` — the row names another ISO's own
 *       market object (a foreign ScenarioConfig field stem, or a foreign
 *       region/programme name: wtx_ path15_ tsa_ rdt_tcdc wecc_endogenous_node)
 *       AND every non-owner ISO's cell reads `.` at HEAD. A foreign-stemmed
 *       row that some OTHER ISO HAS entered is a live cross-ISO question, so
 *       NWPP reads `U` there, not `.` (e.g. ercot_wind_zone_shape,
 *       miso_intermediate_gas_offer_margin, pjm_midcurve_belt,
 *       caiso_p1_export_sink_seam, ercot_storage_adaptive_expectation).
 *   (b) NO CENTRALIZED FORWARD CAPACITY AUCTION -> `.` in BOTH lanes (no
 *       `fc`) — SIX rows: capacity_market_clearing,
 *       capacity_market_supply_clearing, capacity_going_forward_bar_published,
 *       capacity_no_default_cap_convention, net_cone_forward_vintages,
 *       locality_capacity_curves. The footprint is vertically integrated and
 *       dispatches against IRPs and bilateral contracts; WRAP is a forward
 *       SHOWING obligation, not an auction that clears a price.
 *   (c) FORECAST-ONLY ROW (base `mode: "F"`) -> `cell: "."` + `fc: "U"` — a
 *       forecast mechanism has no backcast posture. NWPP has NO forecast-lane
 *       entry at HEAD: that is W6 / card N9, ROUTED to the capx director, and
 *       this shard is not the forecast board.
 *   otherwise -> `U`.
 * `.` is the STRONGER claim (it forecloses a lever), so every row this
 * session could not place with a stated structural reason falls through to
 * `U`, the weaker one — including the hydro family that is this program's
 * structural core (hydro_budget_period_by_instrument, hydro_dispatch_envelope,
 * hydro_min_flow_floor, hydro_ror_split, hydro_budget_nameplate_aware,
 * hydro_level_923_hy, hydro_vintage_input_repair — cards N3 / NWPP-32 /
 * NWPP-36), the seam and import-price rows that lever NWPP-56 will enter
 * (priced_interchange, reference_price_interface, import_hub_pricing,
 * import_shape_lever, seam_neighbour_*_ladder, measured_interface_limits),
 * and the genuinely open ones (capacity_deliverability, lcr_tsl_published,
 * m2m_seam_entitlement_cap, mass_cap_lp_row, legacy_p2). A later NWPP lane
 * closes those on NWPP's own data (rule 25), never by reading another column.
 *
 * TWO REASONS THE CHARTER OFFERED THAT THIS SEED DID **NOT** USE, recorded so
 * nobody reads their absence as an oversight (the `.`-is-stronger discipline
 * above is the whole reason):
 *   - "no reserve co-optimisation" foreclosed ZERO cells. Every reserves row
 *     in the base set is a requirement, pool, scoping or write-only instrument
 *     row, not a market-cleared AS price or a published reserve demand curve —
 *     and `model/reserves/spec.py` takes an NWPP entry at W2 (plan §2.3, per
 *     cards N5/N7), so each of those objects exists for NWPP. All eight read
 *     `U`.
 *   - "no offer-curve tuning channel" foreclosed ZERO cells.
 *     `offer_curve_by_group` is the shared per-class band CONTAINER every ISO
 *     carries; NWPP's bands sit at 1.0, which is a VALUE, not an absence, and
 *     gate G5 states it as the desk's posture "unless the owner rules
 *     otherwise" — a posture cannot carry the stronger `.` claim. It reads
 *     `U`.
 *
 * ONE CELL DIVERGES FROM THE SPP SEED THIS SHARD WAS EMITTED AGAINST:
 * state_carbon_pricing reads `U` here where SPP reads `.`. SPP's reason is
 * that no state in its footprint carries a carbon programme; that reason does
 * not hold for NWPP (Washington's Climate Commitment Act cap-and-invest, in
 * effect since 2023-01-01, inside the scored window). See the cell's own `ev`.
 *
 * Owner rulings already reflected in this seed: N1 (sitting #1, 2026-09-13) —
 * all 17 BAs, key `NWPP`, NEVP in, Canada out. N3 (sitting #1) — the Columbia
 * hydraulic coupling is BUILT BEFORE the first keeper as W3b / NWPP-36, so
 * lever NWPP-54 is RETIRED from the W5 queue and is NOT seeded into §5.9.
 * Cards N4-N8 and N10 are served at sitting #2 and are NOT pre-empted here;
 * where one of them lands against a `.` above, its own lane re-opens the cell.
 *
 * Append NWPP column re-stamp history as block comments at the END of this
 * file.
 */
window.MECH_MATRIX_SHARDS = window.MECH_MATRIX_SHARDS || {};
