    coal_sync_online_frac_per_year: { cell: "U", ev: "MINTED U by the rule-28(c) same-PR duty only (pjm-h15, 2026-09-20) \u2014 NO adjudication is made or implied here, and rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean PJM's evidence never fills this cell. PREREQUISITES for any lane that wants it: this ISO must HAVE the companion artifact thermal_tranches_online_frac_by_year_<ISO>.csv (only MISO and, from this lane, PJM do), and its keeper must arm the coal synchronization floor at all (coal_sync_srmc_tranche AND coal_mustrun_online_pmin) or the flag solves a bit-identical control." },
    mustrun_online_frac_per_year: { cell: "U", ev: "NWPP-21 (2026-09-13) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/nwpp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row NWPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. NWPP is not registered at this commit (`_ISO_BUILDERS` carries seven keys; W2 / NWPP-20 flips the pin), has no keeper, no bundle and no solve of any kind, so nothing here is measured; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.9." },
    coal_sync_window_commitment_grain: { cell: "U", ev: "ROW ADDED 2026-09-22 (pjm-h16) with the field, per rule 28(c) \u2014 U: UNTESTED here, and NO adjudication is made or implied. The chartering measurement is PJM's OWN coal online-hour-of-day census from CAMPD (peak-to-mean of P(online | hour-of-day), metered starts, and the hour-vs-day sharp test); rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean PJM's verdict fills no other ISO's cell, and a lane arming this must first measure its OWN coal fleet's commitment diurnal shape and its own metered start count." },
    mustrun_window_commitment_grain: { cell: "U", ev: "NWPP-21 (2026-09-13) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/nwpp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row NWPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. NWPP is not registered at this commit (`_ISO_BUILDERS` carries seven keys; W2 / NWPP-20 flips the pin), has no keeper, no bundle and no solve of any kind, so nothing here is measured; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.9." },
    coal_sync_ensemble_level: { cell: "U", ev: "MINTED U by the rule-28(c) same-PR duty only (SPP-71, 2026-09-22) -- NO adjudication is made or implied here, and rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean SPP's evidence never fills this cell. PREREQUISITE for any lane that wants it: this ISO's keeper must arm the coal synchronization floor at all (coal_sync_srmc_tranche AND coal_mustrun_online_pmin) or the flag solves a bit-identical control. The question it asks is whether this ISO's coal cyclers should carry pmin x online_frac in every hour instead of full pmin on the top online_frac fraction of hours -- derive the answer from this ISO's own thermal_tranches artifact and its own measured fleet minimum." },
    commitment_floor_window_netload: { cell: "U", ev: "MINTED U by the rule-28(c) same-PR duty only (SPP-66, 2026-09-20) — NO NWPP adjudication is made or implied, and rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean SPP's evidence never fills this cell. The field ships default OFF and NWPP's committed bundles are byte-identical (measured: all 19 committed run configs re-key identically, and the field is registered in _CACHE_KEY_OPTIONAL_FIELDS at 'False'). REACH NOTE: NWPP's committed bundle arms neither coal gate; reach here is limited to the per-plant gas floors and the CT must-run, if armed. Whether net load is the right window driver here is NWPP's own lane's question, to be answered from NWPP's OWN measured fleet behaviour, never transferred from SPP's." },
