    coal_takeorpay_committed: { cell: "K", ev: "NWPP-44 (2026-09-20) PROMOTED \u2014 K: KEEPER, with a gate regression carried on the record. ARM: coal_takeorpay_from_data + coal_committed_takeorpay_regulated for NWPP in pipeline/backcast_config.py. ZERO free parameters (rules 21/24) \u2014 the discount is each plant's own MEASURED EIA-923 Schedule-5 contracted share (data/raw/_processed-legacy/coal_takeorpay_NWPP.csv, 13 of 17 plants, fleet 94% contract on tonnage) and the scope is the published EIA-860 Regulatory Status == RE boolean; build_dof_ledger adds one entry, identification measured-physical, and the 3 residual entries are unchanged from NWPP-40/41/42. SCOPE FIXED EX ANTE BY OWNER RULING 2026-09-20 (PRECOMMIT-nwpp-43 \u00a77): Option B, ALL regulated coal, so coal_prb_committed_dispatchable is NOT armed \u2014 the HARDER option, ruled rather than chosen, because NWPP's measured conduct does not discriminate between ranks (p25\u2192median CF spread ~9-20 pts in both) and picking the carve-out that makes a gate pass is the fitted-mechanism selection rule 1 [R-STRUCT] forbids. MEASURED OFFER DELTA: 13 LP rows move of 641-646, NON-COAL ROWS MOVED 0, |\u0394 pmax| 0.000000 MW, 2,888.8 MW, identical in all three years; two-sided \u2014 the spot-heavy plants' must-run band gets DEARER (North Valmy $4.50\u2192$27.47 on its measured 0.5611 share). DISPATCH: coal displaces gas ONE-FOR-ONE (2025 coal +6.692 TWh vs gas -6.694) with hydro/nuclear/wind/solar unchanged to 0.000 TWh. GATES vs the NWPP-42 keeper: C1 PASS\u2192FAIL, C2 PASS, C4 FAIL\u2192FAIL, C6 PASS, C8 PASS; NOT-YET\u2192NOT-YET. THE REGRESSION: C1 fails on ONE row, 2023 CC_REGULAR -8.22 TWh / -2.3 pp (17/18 pass), PREDICTED in PRECOMMIT \u00a76.2 before any solve as the row that absorbs coal's displacement. Promoted under rule 14 [R-ACCURATE]: a measured input that worsens the fit is a discovered bug elsewhere, never a reason to restore the estimate \u2014 the CC_REGULAR gap is ROUTED, not absorbed. WHAT IMPROVES: C4 coal r 0.570/0.559/0.524\u21920.605/0.595/0.610, NRMSE 0.292/0.387/0.408\u21920.260/0.246/0.284 (inside the 0.30 gate in all three years; C4 still FAILS on the 0.70 r floor); coal volume error sum|err| 25.574\u219210.866 TWh (-57%). PRE-REGISTERED KILL CONDITION SURVIVED: 2024 COAL_BIT +4.898 TWh (\u22652.0), 12.381 against a 14.83 trigger and a 12.832 actual, all C1 coal rows in band. DOES NOT CLOSE the rising-curve defect (NWPP-43 \u00a74.1): it enlarges the cheap block rather than building a stack. The miso-96 objection is ANSWERED in PRECOMMIT \u00a73 on regulatory conduct vs contract accounting, with where it lands recorded. Rules 25/28(d): NOTHING transferred from MISO; every other ISO's cell is untouched. Records: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-nwpp-44-2026-09-20.md, docs/handoffs/RESULT-nwpp-44-2026-09-20.md, docs/FINDING-nwpp44-reuse-solved-cannot-regenerate-shared-2026-09-20.md." },
