    committed_band_measured_basis: { cell: "U", ev: "NWPP-46 (2026-09-22) MEASURED ZERO-LP AND DELIBERATELY NOT ARMED \u2014 the cell stays U because NO LP WAS SPENT ON IT and nothing here is a solved result; it is recorded as DO-NOT-REDO evidence (rule 28(a)) so a successor does not spend a span learning it. The lane was chartered to close C4 on the coal offer stack's vertical extent. TWO MEASUREMENTS ON NWPP'S OWN DATA REFUTE THAT ROUTE. (1) THE PREMISE IS A MIX ARTIFACT: rebuilding the keeper fleet through replay_keeper (run_year(fleet_only=True), scripts/probes/_nwpp46_coal_stack_phase0.py) shows econlo == econhi == peak EXACTLY, to the cent, at ALL 17 NWPP coal plants. The '$0.51/MWh shelf' carried by NWPP-43 \u00a74.1 and the keeper note is the difference between FLEET AVERAGES over different plant mixes, not a slope any plant offers. Cause: backcast_config.py:2372 deep-merges _SPP_OFFER_CURVE, whose _SPP_COAL_IDENTITY_BANDS are 1.0 on EVERY band, for iso in ('SPP','NWPP') \u2014 a posture declared by lane NWPP-20 before any NWPP solve existed to avoid transplanting ERCOT's fitted bands under rule 25, while GENERIC_BASE_OFFER_CURVE['COAL_BIT'] is itself sloped (econ_low 0.95 / econ_high 1.10 / peak 1.45). (2) THE CORRECT LADDER IS SMALL AND WOULD BE INERT. Reproducing the shared WP-3 construction of scripts/data/derive_campd_marginal_hr.py band-for-band over 511,855 steady-state coal unit-hours from NWPP's own CEMS 2023-2025 (scripts/probes/_nwpp46_marginal_hr_phase0.py; two declared departures \u2014 the class map comes from NWPP's own rebuilt fleet because bin_assignments_NWPP.csv does not exist per owner ruling N8, and it reports per plant) gives cap-weighted marg_committed 0.821 / marg_econ_low 0.932 / marg_econ_high 1.004 / marg_peak 1.029, i.e. econ_high/econ_low = 1.077 (p25 1.052 / p50 1.082 / p75 1.123; 17 of 24 units above 1.05). That is a 7.7% rise across the economic range and 10.4% across the whole dispatchable range \u2014 about $3/MWh on a $35 offer, not the 0.9-1.7 GW of missing diurnal swing. AND IT WOULD NOT MATTER: NWPP-INLAND / NWPP-NW / NWPP-OR each carry exactly TWELVE distinct P1 prices for the WHOLE YEAR, one per month, median 1 per day, mean within-day swing $0.00 (NWPP-EAST 84/187/218 prices, $1.74-4.06). A coal plant facing a within-month-constant price runs flat-out or not at all for the month whatever ladder its offer carries. The marginal unit is hydro and its monthly-budget dual is a month-constant water value; the defect re-routes to hydro_dispatch_envelope / hydro_min_flow_floor, which this lane armed instead. THE LADDER IS ROUTED, NOT DISMISSED: it is a real measured correction and rule 14 [R-ACCURATE] favours it, but it should be armed AFTER the price acquires intra-day variation, when it can be tested rather than predicted inert. Evidence: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-nwpp-46-2026-09-22.md \u00a7\u00a72-3, docs/handoffs/RESULT-nwpp-46-2026-09-22.md." },
