    coal_prb_proxy_own_iso: { cell: "K", ev: "ARMED ON THE NWPP RECIPE by owner ruling 2026-09-17 (lane NWPP-41), backcast only, via pipeline/backcast_config.py (iso == \"NWPP\"). Landing NWPP's own coal-rank file data/raw/_processed-legacy/coal_supply_NWPP.csv is what closes the C1 taxonomy seam of FINDING-nwpp-40 \u00a77.1 \u2014 the model dispatched all 17 coal plants as the bare COAL class the benchmark has no row for \u2014 but it also lets apply_coal_supply_pricing reach NWPP's NON-REPORTING PRB plants, and the default proxy is ERCOT's (every plant in COAL_PLANT_SUPPLY is in Texas). This flag scopes the pool to NWPP's own four reporters. MEASURED ZERO-LP BEFORE ANY SOLVE (scripts/probes/_nwpp41_coalrank_phase0.py, run_year(fleet_only=True) on the registered bundle's own recipe via the sanctioned replay_keeper path): non-coal offer max|d| $0.0000000000 with 0 rows moved, pmax and availability max|d| exactly 0, in ALL THREE YEARS; 7 coal rows move in 2023/2024 and 11 in 2025, on Colstrip (6076), Hardin (55749) and TS Power (56224, 2025 only \u2014 its 2025 receipt is not yet filed). Colstrip committed 34.252 -> 27.226 / 34.550 -> 25.640 / 34.850 -> 25.640 $/MWh; coal capacity-weighted mean offer -0.653 / -0.828 / -0.886. Against the UNSCOPED alternative Colstrip would have gone to 23.766 / 23.016 / 21.560 \u2014 i.e. the scoping is worth +$2-4/MWh and is the whole point. Zero free parameters; rules 14 [R-ACCURATE] / 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]. Evidence: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-nwpp-41-2026-09-17.md \u00a73. RE-STAMPED AT PROMOTION (2026-09-19): this flag rides NWPP's FIRST keeper (lane NWPP-41; run id pruned at the NWPP-42 promotion and cited by LANE per rule 15). RE-STAMPED AGAIN (2026-09-20, lane NWPP-42): it rides ARMED and UNCHANGED in the current keeper 2026-09-20-nwpp42-measured-coal-heat, whose recipe is NWPP-41's plus one field (measured_coal_heat_rates); nothing about this flag was re-derived or re-measured. THE SOLVE CONFIRMED THE ZERO-LP PREDICTION: no bare COAL class row survives in any year and the itemized family reads 39.6133 / 27.0076 / 27.2069 TWh, so C1 went FAIL (5 rows) -> PASS (18/18 all, 14/14 free) against the lane-NWPP-40 control differenced at rule-29(b) form 4, with NO control solve. Both PRECOMMIT predictions landed: C1 closed, C4 still FAILs. C4's coal r and NRMSE ALSO improved (0.511 / 0.535 / 0.475 -> 0.539 / 0.546 / 0.502 and 0.321 / 0.408 / 0.451 -> 0.301 / 0.397 / 0.432) and the reported-only C5a CO2 error improved sharply (-65.9 / -58.7 / -54.8 % -> -15.1 / -23.7 / -21.4 %, likely per-class emission-rate coverage restored by the taxonomy fix, since less coal would push the error the other way) \u2014 BOTH ARE SIDE EFFECTS REPORTED, NOT ACHIEVEMENTS CLAIMED (rule 1 [R-STRUCT]: no dispatch mechanism was touched). Rule 21 [R-DOF]: build_dof_ledger.py emits 3 entries / 3 residual on this bundle, IDENTICAL to lane NWPP-40's \u2014 the arm added no free parameter, because it selects WHICH measured EIA-923 Schedule-2 series the fallback proxy pools. THE SAME DEFECT REACHES MISO (12 plants), PJM (2) and SPP (3-5) and was DELIBERATELY NOT FIXED: their cells stay O (rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d)). Evidence: docs/handoffs/FINDING-nwpp-41-2026-09-19.md; frontend/data/backcast/keepers/NWPP.json." },
