    hydro_dispatch_envelope: { cell: "K", ev: "NWPP-46 (2026-09-22) PROMOTED BY OWNER RULING \u2014 K: KEEPER. It rides ARMED in NWPP's keeper 2026-09-22-nwpp46-hydro-envelope (bundle results/calibration/nwpp46_hydroenv_span). The cell flips on the RULING, not on any residual (rule 1 [R-STRUCT]); the owner's standing instruction is that structural gains may justify gate regressions, and here NO gate regresses. PRIOR CELL TEXT (kept verbatim): NWPP-46 (2026-09-22) SOLVED ON THE FOOTPRINT, ARMED, REGISTERED, PROMOTION UNRULED \u2014 O: OPEN pending the owner's promotion ruling (rule 31 [R-RETAIN]); flips to K only on that ruling. Run 2026-09-22-nwpp46-hydro-envelope, bundle results/calibration/nwpp46_hydroenv_span, three year-isolated shards (rule 36) composed by the parent; the parent ran ZERO LP (rule 32(a)). ARMED AS ONE MECHANISM WITH hydro_min_flow_floor and never apart: constants.py defines HYDRO_MIN_FLOW_PERCENTILE = 100.0 - HYDRO_ENVELOPE_PERCENTILE, so the two-sided envelope is identified by the ONE percentile the ceiling carries \u2014 ZERO new free parameters (rule 21), ZERO code change (both are existing ScenarioConfig fields on the calibration CLI, rule 24). RULE 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]: NOTHING transferred from CAISO \u2014 the ceiling is the p95 of NWPP's OWN EIA-930 NG:WAT per (month x hour-of-day); the percentile is the shared structural convention. WHY IT WAS ARMED, AND IT IS NOT THE CHARTERED LEVER: the lane was chartered to close C4 on the COAL OFFER STACK's vertical extent and NWPP's own data FALSIFIED that premise twice (PRECOMMIT \u00a7\u00a72-3). (1) Per plant econlo == econhi == peak EXACTLY at all 17 coal plants \u2014 the '$0.51/MWh shelf' in the record is a fleet MIX artifact, not a within-plant slope \u2014 because backcast_config:2372 merges _SPP_OFFER_CURVE (the IDENTITY, 1.0 on every band) for NWPP. (2) NWPP's own CAMPD (511,855 steady-state coal unit-hours, the shared WP-3 construction) meters only a 10.4% ladder across the dispatchable range (~$3/MWh), and it would be INERT anyway because THE PRICE COAL FACES HAS NO INTRA-DAY VARIATION: NWPP-INLAND / NW / OR carry exactly TWELVE distinct prices per YEAR, one per month, median 1 per day, mean within-day swing $0.00. The marginal unit is hydro and its monthly-budget dual is a month-constant water value. MEASURED DEFECT: model hydro runs 114/120/138% of the real diurnal swing while coal runs 10/5/4% and gas 65-69% (solar and wind match at 1.00, so it is not a renewables artifact); on the additive h19-h11 ramp metric hydro's excess accounts for 69/87/102% of the coal+gas ramp deficit. Lever (C) was also closed for free: D-2 reads COAL forced_twh = 0.0 in all three years and D-4 carries no coal row, so there is no coal floor. MEASURED BINDING: 21.7/23.7/23.4% of hours, 1.864/2.359/2.684 TWh above the ceiling, concentrated h16-h22 (29-47% of those hours) \u2014 the perfect-foresight hoarding an energy-only budget cap permits, the same defect caiso-72 names. RESULT: the gate profile is IDENTICAL to the keeper (C1 FAIL, C2 PASS, C4 FAIL, C6 PASS, C8 PASS, NOT-YET) and NO C1 row changed status; DOF ledger 4/3 residual, unchanged from NWPP-40/41/42/44. C4 improves on BOTH metrics in ALL THREE years and STILL FAILS, as predicted ex ante: r 0.605/0.595/0.610 -> 0.658/0.617/0.637 against a 0.70 floor, NRMSE 0.260/0.246/0.284 -> 0.244/0.240/0.276; coal diurnal amplitude ratio 0.100/0.052/0.037 -> 0.223/0.096/0.089, roughly DOUBLED every year. THE PRE-REGISTERED KILL CONDITION WAS CODED AND COMMITTED BEFORE THE FIRST LEG LANDED (scripts/probes/_nwpp46_gates.py at 9cd108d9) and does NOT fire in either direction: hydro amplitude ratio 1.138/1.200/1.383 -> 1.048/1.107/1.148 against an INERT limb of <1.11/<1.17/<1.35; hydro annual energy moved 0.000 TWh against a 5.0 TWh OVERSHOOT budget; every C1 COAL row inside its \u00b18.00 TWh band. THE EX-ANTE PREDICTION LANDED: PRECOMMIT \u00a76a predicted the hydro ratio at 1.05/1.10/1.16 from a static clip and the solve returned 1.048/1.107/1.148 (within 0.002/0.007/0.012); every C4 r and NRMSE landed INSIDE its predicted band. ONE EX-ANTE PREDICTION WAS WRONG AND IS REPORTED AS SUCH: \u00a76e predicted 2023 CC_REGULAR would IMPROVE; it moved 0.422 TWh FURTHER OUT (-8.219 -> -8.641), because hydro energy was exactly conserved so there was no released volume for the marginal class to absorb. ALSO REPORTED BECAUSE IT COMPLICATES THE STORY: r_intra rose only in 2023 (0.218 -> 0.371); it is flat in 2024 (0.376 -> 0.375) and WORSE in 2025 (0.425 -> 0.374) \u2014 the arm fixed the SIZE of the swing more than its HOUR. Rule 1 [R-STRUCT]: C4 was never the reason to arm this and is not a promotion criterion in either direction. Evidence: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-nwpp-46-2026-09-22.md, docs/handoffs/RESULT-nwpp-46-2026-09-22.md, scripts/probes/_nwpp46_{coal_stack,marginal_hr,hydro_envelope}_phase0.py, scripts/probes/_nwpp46_gates.py." },
    hydro_min_flow_floor: { cell: "K", ev: "NWPP-46 (2026-09-22) PROMOTED BY OWNER RULING \u2014 K: KEEPER, armed WITH hydro_dispatch_envelope as one mechanism and never apart. PRIOR CELL TEXT (kept verbatim): NWPP-46 (2026-09-22) SOLVED, ARMED, REGISTERED, PROMOTION UNRULED \u2014 O: OPEN pending the owner's ruling (rule 31); flips to K only on that ruling. THE LOWER HALF of the same two-sided measured capability envelope as hydro_dispatch_envelope, armed WITH it and never apart (rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]); see that cell for the full result. It adds ZERO free parameters on top of the ceiling: HYDRO_MIN_FLOW_PERCENTILE is defined as 100.0 - HYDRO_ENVELOPE_PERCENTILE, and read as an exceedance level it is Q95, the hydrological low-flow index environmental / FERC minimum-flow licence conditions are themselves written against. Level from NWPP's OWN EIA-930 NG:WAT per CALENDAR MONTH \u2014 the month ALONE, never (month x hour-of-day), because a floor carrying the measured diurnal shape would pin dispatch to the measured outcome (rule 13 [R-MEASURED]). RULE 17 [R-FLOOR-WINDOW]: (a) driver \u2014 run-of-river inflow that cannot be stored plus the licence minimum releases the energy-only budget cap ignores; (b) window \u2014 all 24 h, and D-4 scores off-window share 0.0 in every year; (c) forward story \u2014 re-derives from the pooled HYDRO_CLIMATOLOGY_YEARS percentile and responds to the water year through the budget it is clipped against. MEASURED BINDING: 10.4/12.9/14.0% of hours, 0.866/1.185/1.526 TWh below the sustained level, concentrated in the MIDDAY SOLAR BELLY and the OVERNIGHT SHOULDER \u2014 DISJOINT from the ceiling's evening hours, which is the rule-19 evidence that the two are one reconciled family and not a stack. C8 IS NOT AT RISK AND DID NOT MOVE: MECH_HYDRO_MIN_FLOW is classed NON-THERMAL forcing (water, not a commitment decision), so D-2 REPORTS it \u2014 52.989/55.847/57.754 TWh, 49.6/51.8/51.1% of hydro, against CAISO's own 36-46% \u2014 but excludes it from the merchant thermal forced-share arithmetic; C8 reads PASS with forced_share 0.0 on every gated thermal class. Hydro annual energy is unchanged to 0.000 TWh in all three years, the direct evidence that the two-sided envelope is a SHAPE constraint and not a volume mechanism. Evidence: as the ceiling cell." },
    hydro_ror_split: { cell: "U", ev: "NWPP-21 (2026-09-13) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/nwpp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row NWPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. NWPP is not registered at this commit (`_ISO_BUILDERS` carries seven keys; W2 / NWPP-20 flips the pin), has no keeper, no bundle and no solve of any kind, so nothing here is measured; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.9." },
